DESCRIPTION:Storing build artifacts allows us to quickly and repeatedly dep
	loy previous commits to an environment. This is essential to rollback func
	tionality. This also can help ensure that if a piece of functionality work
	s in Test\, it will also work in Prod. However\, our Test and Prod environ
	ments are set up differently. This meeting is to explore the differences i
	n Test and Prod\, and determine how the build artifacts should be formatte
	d to benefit both environments.\n\nWe need to determine:\n\n1.	\n	Build ar
	tifact layout/format - Multiple artifacts (one for each repo) or match for
	mat of web servers\n2.	Look into deployed differences between Test vs Prod
	\, and come up with a strategy on how the artifact should look to be able 
	to deploy to either env\n3.	Determine the build artifacts retention policy
	 (first pass\, can refine later)\n\n\n____________________________________
	____________________________________________\nMicrosoft Teams Need help? <
