DESCRIPTION: \n\nThanks in advance to everyone for taking time away from th
	eir families to help with this move!\n\nThe hope is that everything will g
	o smoothly and we won’t even take the full hour.\n\n\nHere are the high 
	level steps we will follow this evening to deploy the code:\n\n \n\n*	Corb
	 - Take snap shots of the servers before we move the code.\n\n	*	If any is
	sues are found with the below steps that can’t be fixed quickly\, we wil
	l revert back to the snap shots\n\n*	Doug - Take node 1 out of service and
	 deploy the new code to it.\n*	Doug\, Josh - Point our PCs to the node tha
	t is out of service using our host file.\n*	Doug\, Josh - Test a few pages
	 on the node that is out of service to see if things look to be working.\n
	*	Decision point - Is the site working with the new code?\n*	Josh - Simula
	te a large amount of requests to the site that is out of service.\n*	Doug 
	- Monitor the socket usage on the node that is out of service. \n*	Decisio
	n point - Are we happy with the socket usage and can we make this live to 
	the public?\n*	Doug - Put node 1 back in service. \n*	Doug - Take node 2 o
	ut of service. \n*	Doug\, Josh - Remove the host file entry \n*	Doug\, Jos
	h - Test a few pages on dmba.com to see if things still look to be working
	.\n*	Decision point - Is everything working correctly? Are we ready to mov
	e both nodes live.\n*	Doug - Deploy the new code to node 2\n*	Doug - Put n
	ode 2 back in service\n*	Doug\, Josh - Monitor the site for errors (this w
	ill be ongoing for the next couple of days)\n*	Larsen - Run some socket te
	sts to verify the fix is working. (This will happen later in the evening w
	hen he is available)\n\n \n\n \n\n________________________________________
	________________________________________\n\nMicrosoft Teams Need help? <ht
