	y lang="EN-US" link="#467886" vlink="#96607D" style="word-wrap:break-word"
	><div class="WordSection1"><p class="MsoNormal">Let’s get together and c
	ontinue our conversation on help desk tickets and troubleshooting issues. 
	<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">For this first one\, we will go over S
	plunk and some of the ways to use it. <o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">
	Here are a few that I thought of:<o:p></o:p></p><ul style="margin-top:0in"
	 type="disc"><li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-list:l0 level1 lfo3">Looking
	 up errors based on day and time<o:p></o:p></li><li class="MsoNormal" styl
	e="mso-list:l0 level1 lfo3">Looking up errors by tracing a web login<o:p><
	/o:p></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-list:l0 level1 lfo3">Looking up
	 matching events in the event viewer<o:p></o:p></li><li class="MsoNormal" 
	style="mso-list:l0 level1 lfo3">Looking up API errors and bad requests<o:p
	></o:p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp\;</o:p></p><p class="MsoN
	ormal">If there are any other topics on Splunk you want to go over\, send 
	them to me via chat and I will add them to the list.<o:p></o:p></p><p clas
