DESCRIPTION:Simplified Agenda (90 min)\n\n1.	Kickoff & Goals (5) — align 
	scope\, slice work\, load next 2 sprints\n2.	Elevated Access (“Break Gla
	ss”) (25) \n\n	*	Decide v1 scope (salary‑only vs broader PHI screens)\
	n	*	Confirm Admin app MVP + shared modal pattern (MVC/WebForms/Classic ASP
	)\n	*	Estimate story points for each user story (admin app\, modal compone
	nt(s)\, logging)\n\n3.	RxSS with SSO (20) \n\n	*	Assign owners\; confirm B
	I/vendor dependencies (metadata\, eligibility file\, test env)\n	*	Estimat
	e story points for each user story (metadata exchange\, eligibility file\,
	 link UI\, test flow\, prod cutover)\n\n4.	Bugs Triage (15) — rank new i
	tems\, assign owners (keep it fast)\n5.	Tech Debt (10) — pick 1–2 quic
	k wins\, backlog the rest\n6.	Wrap (5) — owners\, due dates\, comms\n\n_
	_______________________________\n\n🔍 The Scoop (TL\;DR for the team)\
	nElevated Access (“Break Glass”)\n\n*	Full coverage estimate ≈ 211 h
	rs (Admin app .NET 8 + modals across most apps)\n*	Focused v1 (salary‑di
	splaying apps) ≈ 50–60 hrs\n*	Trade‑off: broader audit coverage vs. 
	faster delivery\n*	Today’s calls: lock scope\, standardize modal approac
	h\, story‑point the user stories\n\nIntegrate RxSS with SSO\n\n*	Estimat
	e ≈ 32 hrs (assuming vendor + BI dependencies line up)\n*	Dependencies: 
	metadata exchange\, eligibility file\, vendor test environment\, dmba.com 
	link placement\n*	Today’s calls: assign owner(s)\, confirm dependencies\
	, story‑point the user stories\n\n\n\n__________________________________
