DESCRIPTION:Many of us have created various subagents\, skills\, commands\,
	 etc in Claude Code. Let’s meet and plan which of these assets we want t
	o centralize into a standard “library” and how to share them across ou
	r team. Bring your ideas and the ones you’ve created\, and we’ll discu
	ss and plan together.\n\n \n\nPossible questions for our discussion:\n\n \
	n\n*	What subagents or commands/skills do you think we should have in our 
	shared repo?\n*	What naming convention and standards should we follow for 
	these shared assets?\n*	Where should they be stored?\n*	How do we make the
	m discoverable and documented?\n*	Subagents vs skills/commands\n*	Process 
	for changing and creating new ones\n*	How to differentiate stable vs exper
	imental assets? \n*	Ownership\n*	Scope creep and guardrails – What gets 
	shared and what does not? How do we avoid accumulating too much and creati
	ng a big frakenlibrary?\n*	Assignments and next steps\n\n_________________
	_______________________________________________________________\n\nMicroso
	ft Teams meeting \n\nJoin: https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/24024264152099
	6?p=D8lNjve76Wk9juWBya <https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/ap/
